All active implementation: `vestara-ai-core/`
Blueprint (frozen architecture): `vestara-blueprint/`

## Workflow (VSDE)
1. Read PRODUCT-PRINCIPLES.md and VSDE standard
2. Read relevant Capability Specification Package (CSP)
3. Specifications before implementation — never start coding without a complete CSP
4. Implement against existing contracts (architecture is frozen)
5. Write tests (Vitest, sql.js in-memory)
6. Verify: pnpm test && bash build-order.sh

## Architecture
- WorkspaceRuntime is the orchestration boundary (CLI imports only this)
- RepositoryWorkspace is the canonical domain object
- 22 packages in dependency order (build-order.sh)
- sql.js (WASM) for SQLite — NOT better-sqlite3
- OpenCode is the sole AI provider
- AI is optional — all pipelines degrade gracefully

## Engineering Rules
- Zero any types
- kebab-case for filenames
- No code comments unless asked
- No console.log (use @vestara/logger)
- Every public interface in @vestara/shared
- Event-driven via EventBus (pattern matching with * wildcards)

## NEVER DO
- Modify blueprint documents without ADR
- Add comments unless asked
- Assume better-sqlite3 (use sql.js)
- Add emoji unless explicitly requested
